<figure class="diagram record-length-model">
  <p class="extent-example"><b>Example:</b> This is a server-to-client
  <a href="#chat-message-recv"><code>Chat/11 MessageRecv</code></a> record. The
  diagram shows only the consumed bit counts.</p>

  <div class="extent-flow" aria-label="Five stages used to determine the length of a Sunken record">
    <div class="extent-step extent-route"
      aria-label="Step one: read the eleven-bit routing header">
      <span>1</span><strong>Read route</strong><small>11 bits consumed</small>
    </div>
    <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
    <div class="extent-step extent-schema"
      aria-label="Step two: map the route to the Chat MessageRecv decoder">
      <span>2</span><strong>Select schema</strong><small><code>Chat/11</code> receive</small>
    </div>
    <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
    <div class="extent-step extent-payload"
      aria-label="Step three: the selected payload decoder consumes three hundred thirty-six bits">
      <span>3</span><strong>Decode payload</strong><small>336 bits consumed</small>
    </div>
    <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
    <div class="extent-step extent-padding"
      aria-label="Step four: consume five zero padding bits to reach the next byte boundary">
      <span>4</span><strong>Align record</strong><small>5 zero bits</small>
    </div>
    <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
    <div class="extent-step extent-result"
      aria-label="Step five: the complete record is forty-four bytes">
      <span>5</span><strong>Boundary known</strong><small>44 bytes total</small>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="extent-equation" aria-label="Eleven header bits plus three hundred thirty-six payload bits plus five padding bits equals three hundred fifty-two bits or forty-four bytes">
    <code>11 header</code><b>+</b><code>336 payload</code><b>+</b><code>5 pad</code><b>=</b><code>352 bits</code><b>=</b><code>44 bytes</code>
  </div>

  <div class="extent-explainer">
    <p class="extent-default"><b>The record size is a result.</b> First, the decoder
    reads the route. Then, it applies the payload schema. Finally, it aligns the
    cursor to a byte boundary. The final cursor gives the record size.</p>
  </div>

  <h4>Payload extent</h4>
  <div class="extent-controls">
    <div><strong>Fixed-width value</strong><span>The schema supplies the exact width: for example, one bit for a Boolean or 32 bits for a FourCC.</span></div>
    <div><strong>Array or byte string</strong><span>A bounded local count is decoded first. It determines the number of elements or raw bytes that follow.</span></div>
    <div><strong>Optional value</strong><span>One presence bit decides whether the nested value follows.</span></div>
    <div><strong>Choice</strong><span>A bounded selector chooses one arm; only that arm is decoded.</span></div>
    <div><strong>Structure</strong><span>Members are decoded recursively in generated wire order until the structure is complete.</span></div>
    <div><strong>Alignment point</strong><span>A string or blob can align to the next byte before its raw bytes. Final padding aligns the top-level value.</span></div>
  </div>
</figure>
